and it was all women.

00:07:58.020 --> 00:08:00.030
Yeah. It was unbelievable.

00:08:00.030 --> 00:08:02.340
Vanessa Williams, Susie Mcara.

00:08:02.340 --> 00:08:04.229
And like, it was just amazing.

00:08:04.229 --> 00:08:05.062
(audience clapping)

00:08:05.062 --> 00:08:08.670
But the best part is
the title of the play.

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:12.418
So, the title is called Potus
or Behind Every Great Dumbass

00:08:12.418 --> 00:08:15.034
or Seven Women Trying to Keep 'em Alive.

00:08:15.034 --> 00:08:16.770
(everyone laughing)

00:08:16.770 --> 00:08:19.020
- And it's like the longest
title, but it's extremely funny.

00:08:19.020 --> 00:08:20.100
- It is. It's a farce.

00:08:20.100 --> 00:08:22.410
And you know what was so
great about it is, you know?

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:24.192
Last year with everything going on.

00:08:24.192 --> 00:08:26.520
I mean, politically it
was like, we thought we

00:08:26.520 --> 00:08:29.970
were coming in to do a, a
comedy and at some point

00:08:29.970 --> 00:08:32.820
like it switched and all of a
sudden it was very cathartic

00:08:32.820 --> 00:08:34.920
and people were coming in
and it was so, like we were

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.710
in this moment of time and
history and it was just

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:41.340
the first time I've ever been
able to like really stand

00:08:41.340 --> 00:08:44.070
for what I believe in through my art.

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:46.140
Instead of having to like,
you know, get on Instagram

00:08:46.140 --> 00:08:48.810
and preach, you know, it was
like, this is what I believe in

00:08:48.810 --> 00:08:50.070
and I get to do it through my art.

00:08:50.070 --> 00:08:51.660
And that was really, really cool.

00:08:51.660 --> 00:08:52.770
- And it's the coolest thing too.

00:08:52.770 --> 00:08:54.090
To be able to do that with humor.

00:08:54.090 --> 00:08:54.923
- [Julianne] Yes.

00:08:54.923 --> 00:08:56.460
- Because that's how you,
you, you break the barrier.

00:08:56.460 --> 00:08:58.500
I feel like between if any divisional kind

00:08:58.500 --> 00:08:59.333
of thing happening.

00:08:59.333 --> 00:09:00.190
- Exactly. Exactly.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:01.350
- [Kelly] Any division
happening, I should say.

00:09:01.350 --> 00:09:04.080
But it, I feel like that
humor just comes right in

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:04.913
to save the day.

00:09:04.913 --> 00:09:08.100
And it's like, it makes
you kind of step back

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:08.933
and just see things

00:09:08.933 --> 00:09:11.040
from different sides
and like a playful way.

00:09:11.040 --> 00:09:13.320
- Well, and obviously it
can always get very heavy

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:15.330
and so the fact that
there was like a moment

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:17.940
where you could go to a
play and have real issues,

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:21.000
but you're laughing and feeling
so empowered when you leave.

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.590
Like that was so special.

00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:24.870
- And thought-provoking, it's
cool to be part of something.

00:09:24.870 --> 00:09:27.300
I assume that it is
thought-provoking and people leave.

00:09:27.300 --> 00:09:28.133
- [Julianne] It is.

00:09:28.133 --> 00:09:28.966
- Talking.

00:09:28.966 --> 00:09:29.800
- It is.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:30.633
- That's so cool.

00:09:30.633 --> 00:09:31.466
- Yeah, it is.

00:09:31.466 --> 00:09:33.450
- Well, everyone has a story
about something not going right

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:34.530
like with a live show.

00:09:34.530 --> 00:09:35.363
- [Julianne] Oh yeah.

00:09:35.363 --> 00:09:36.527
- I have plenty.

00:09:36.527 --> 00:09:37.360
(everyone laughing)

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:38.193
And I've shared a lot of them.

00:09:38.193 --> 00:09:39.870
What is yours if like in a dancing thing

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:40.703
or whatever you're doing?

00:09:40.703 --> 00:09:41.735
- [Julianne] Oh my gosh.

00:09:41.735 --> 00:09:43.290
- Has anything ever gone very poorly?

00:09:43.290 --> 00:09:45.510
- [Julianne] I mean,
wardrobe malfunctions.

00:09:45.510 --> 00:09:47.463
Like up the yin yang, literally.

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.400
And like, I don't know.

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:53.280
I mean, I definitely
have not forgotten a line

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.736
but forgotten to speak and you know.

00:09:55.736 --> 00:09:56.580
- [Kelly] Interesting.

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:59.580
- Like meaning like, I
just forgot it was my turn.

00:09:59.580 --> 00:10:00.413
- Oh, okay.

00:10:00.413 --> 00:10:04.530
- You know, and so like, there
was a pause and then, huh.

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:07.530
You know? Which is like the
biggest dream that you have.

00:10:07.530 --> 00:10:08.363
Like nightmare.

00:10:08.363 --> 00:10:09.196
- [Kelly] Nightmare. Yeah.

00:10:09.196 --> 00:10:10.170
- That like, you forget your lines.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:11.820
You can't sing like you're dancing

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:13.530
and you're falling on the
floor and you can't get

00:10:13.530 --> 00:10:15.240
up. Like, those are my
nightmares by the way.

00:10:15.240 --> 00:10:16.073
You're welcome.

00:10:16.073 --> 00:10:18.870
Yeah. But that actually happened

00:10:18.870 --> 00:10:21.300
on stage where I just like, I just froze.

00:10:21.300 --> 00:10:23.430
Cause I was like, yeah, who's
supposed to speak right now?

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:24.990
- Why is it someone's failing here?

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:26.820
- Yeah. Someone sucks.

00:10:26.820 --> 00:10:28.080
Not, oh, it's me.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:30.300
- I forget lines all the time.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:33.120
Like I, even whenever I was
like high school doing musical

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:35.940
like theater, like I, I always messed it.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.440
I just kind of would improv it.

00:10:37.440 --> 00:10:38.850
But I do the same thing musically.

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:40.860
I think my memory isn't great with stuff

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.840
like that, so I just end up
making it up in the moment.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:45.900
- Yeah. Actually I do, you just
made me think of something.

00:10:45.900 --> 00:10:46.733
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:10:46.733 --> 00:10:47.940
- When I was touring
and doing country music

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.850
I forgot the lyrics to
my own song that I wrote.

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:53.850
- It specifically the
ones you write, you write.

00:10:53.850 --> 00:10:54.780
- [Julianne] Yeah. Yeah.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:55.613
- What is that?

00:10:55.613 --> 00:10:56.446
- I don't know.

00:10:56.446 --> 00:10:57.279
- Yeah

00:10:57.279 --> 00:10:58.112
- Like we weren't certain.

00:10:58.112 --> 00:11:00.060
Like we had so many
ideas for maybe this line

00:11:00.060 --> 00:11:01.890
that we couldn't remember
which one we went with.

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.671
Like, I don't know what happens, but

00:11:03.671 --> 00:11:04.504
- [Julianne] Totally.

00:11:04.504 --> 00:11:05.850
- It's the worst when it's your song.

00:11:05.850 --> 00:11:07.800
Yeah, and then you're just like, you sing.

00:11:07.800 --> 00:11:09.587
- [Julianne] Yeah.

00:11:09.587 --> 00:11:11.343
- Or like, I meant to do this yeah.

